# The Pi runs the daily poll and this box still ingests by hand, so the same
# file gets written on Linux and on Windows. Several publishers' writers emit
# CRLF deliberately (build_forward_forecast.py says so in a comment); on
# Windows autocrlf normalised that away on commit and on the Pi it did not, so
# the first scheduled run rewrote a forecast file end to end with no change to
# a single figure (2026-09-03). The archive is stored LF — 300 sampled blobs,
# all LF — so pin it there and let either machine write what it likes on disk.
public/data/**/*.json text eol=lf
lib/available-dates.json text eol=lf

# Executable as checked out, whichever machine clones it.
scripts/pi-*.sh text eol=lf
